  "goodToKnow": "Der Elfmeter (colloquially der Elfer, officially der Strafstoß) is a penalty kick, taken from eleven metres, the German rounding of the 12-yard mark. Germany has a famous record in penalty shoot-outs (Elfmeterschießen): it has never lost one at a World Cup, and in 2006 goalkeeper Jens Lehmann used a note in his sock against Argentina. Gary Lineker's quip about Germans always winning is well known. Plural: die Elfmeter."
